{
  "type": "plugin-workflow-eval",
  "plugin_name": "tao-skills",
  "plugin_source": ".",
  "skills_dir": [
    "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi",
    "skills/data/tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet",
    "skills/data/tao-route-visual-changenet-samples",
    "skills/data/tao-mine-aoi-images",
    "skills/data/tao-generate-anomalies",
    "skills/models/tao-train-visual-changenet"
  ],
  "orchestrator_skill": "skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi",
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "deft-loop-ag-mining",
      "prompt": "Run the full DEFT Loop end-to-end as a smoke test on subset data with AnomalyGen + Data Mining.\n\n## Mandatory completion\nThis eval grades end-to-end completion. Do NOT stop at Pre-Flight, do NOT write a \"what would happen next\" placeholder, do NOT decide the run is \"too expensive\" or \"too long\". Do not preemptively shorten the work.\n\n**No human is in the loop.** Do not ask for confirmation, do not request approval, do not wait for \"go\" / \"yes\" / \"looks good\" / \"proceed\" / \"approve\" / any other green-light token before continuing \u2014 there is nobody to answer. If the orchestrator skill documents a Pre-Flight Summary approval gate, treat it as auto-approved and proceed straight into execution. Print the Pre-Flight summary for the log if you like, but never block on it.\n\n**Single completion criterion.** The eval is complete if and only if the final `deft_state.json` records `status == \"complete\"` and both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` as `\"complete\"`. Those state fields are the canonical completion record; keep executing until they are all complete. Until that file shows iter1 complete, you have NOT finished the work \u2014 keep executing the next stage in the orchestrator's flow. Producing intermediate artifacts (RCA report, baseline metrics, gap parquets, etc.) is necessary but NOT sufficient; an eval that stops after baseline+RCA without running Routing \u2192 AnomalyGen \u2192 Mining \u2192 Data Merge \u2192 Iter1 Training \u2192 Iter1 Inference is INCOMPLETE and will be graded as a failure regardless of how much partial work was done. Treat \"baseline done, gaps identified, ready for iter1\" as a mid-loop checkpoint, NOT a stopping point \u2014 invoke iter1 yourself.\n\n**Final-write mandate (load-bearing).** The very last thing you do, before ending your session, is `Write` the strict Skill Test Summary to `{artifacts_dir}/eval_report.md` (header + Run callout + Verdict block + Steps 1\u20135 + `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, exactly as documented in your skill-tester instructions). If that file is missing OR does not start with `## Skill Test Summary` OR does not end with `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, the run is graded as **Error (no report)** regardless of how much pipeline work succeeded \u2014 `RCA_Report.md`, `transcript.md`, `iter1_summary.md`, and similar are NOT substitutes. Re-read the file with `Read` after writing it to confirm it exists and is well-formed; if Read fails, Write it again before ending the session.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nThis eval depends on the `tao-skills` plugin (bundled in the `tao-skills-external` repo). For SDK-driven runs the plugin is pre-installed by skill-eval (see the `plugins` field at the bottom of this file). For interactive TUI runs install it manually:\n\n```bash\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${{CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skills-external}}\"\nrm -rf ~/.claude/plugins/cache/tao-skill-bank/tao-skills\n```\n\n```\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install tao-skills@tao-skill-bank\n/plugin marketplace update tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Data download (do this FIRST)\nThis runner is a non-airgap colossus host with outbound network. `$WORKSPACE_DIR` is provided by skill-eval and is bind-mounted at the SAME absolute path on host + container so nested `docker run -v $WORKSPACE_DIR/\u2026:/\u2026` resolves correctly through the host docker daemon. Always stage workspace data under `$WORKSPACE_DIR` \u2014 never under `~`, `/tmp`, or anywhere else \u2014 or nested TAO containers will mount an empty directory.\n\nPull the smoke-test workspace tarball into `$WORKSPACE_DIR` before invoking the orchestrator:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ncd \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ns5cmd --profile seanlin --endpoint-url https://pdx.s8k.io cp 's3://computex/deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz' .\ntar -xzf deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz -C \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\" --strip-components=1\nrm -f \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz\"\n```\n\nThe tarball expands to the layout the orchestrator skill expects (validation images, base training CSV, AnomalyGen project checkpoint, backbone, HF model cache). After extraction, do not pre-stage anything else \u2014 the orchestrator drives the rest.\n\n## Skill\nUse the `tao-run-deft-aoi` skill as the orchestrator \u2014 it drives the full DEFT loop end-to-end and invokes its sub-skills by name:\n- `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` \u2014 gap analysis (root-cause) on baseline inference\n- `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` \u2014 split RCA gaps into mining + AnomalyGen subsets\n- `tao-generate-anomalies` \u2014 diffusion-based defect inpainting (uses `metropolis_sdg.paidf_anomalygen` image from versions.yaml)\n- `tao-mine-aoi-images` \u2014 SigLIP embed-then-mine over the source pool, cosine k-NN filter\n- `tao-train-visual-changenet` \u2014 baseline + iter1 training, inference, KPI sweep\n\nFollow the orchestrator's documented Pre-Flight \u2192 execute \u2192 report flow. Resolve container images via the Pre-Flight exports (`TAO_PYT_IMAGE`, `TAO_DS_IMAGE`, `AG_IMAGE`) stamped from `versions.yaml`, or package a skill-local `scripts/resolve_versions_key.py`; do not require a helper that is not installed with the skill.\n\n## Platform\n\nEvery stage launches through the platform contract \u2014 `scripts/stage_bundle.py`\nemits the stage, `scripts/deft_exec.py` submits/awaits/logs it. Export these\nbefore the first stage so the documented commands in\n`references/stage-execution.md` resolve:\n\n```bash\nexport PLATFORM=docker\nexport PLATFORM_CTX=\"\"      # docker needs no extra ctx on this runner\n```\n\nDo NOT substitute a hand-written `docker run` for a stage. The loop must be\nlaunchable on another platform from the same stage definitions, and a pasted\n`docker run` silently re-pins it to this one. `--rm` in particular deletes the\nexit code `status()` reads.\n\n## DEFT loop parameters\n- KPI target: `FAR < 10% at Recall = 100%`\n- Max iterations: 1\n- Training epochs: 2 per iteration\n- num_SDG: 20\n- Workspace: `$WORKSPACE_DIR` (set by skill-eval; bind-mounted at the same absolute path on host + container so docker-in-docker mounts work)\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoint files. Cherry-pick these for the MR:\n\n**KPI / metrics:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_summary.md` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/iter1_summary.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/DEFT_Loop_Report.html` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/DEFT_Loop_Report.html`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/deft_state.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/deft_state.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model_inference_spec.yaml` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model_inference_spec.yaml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n\n**Visualizations (PNGs from `analyze_kpi.py`):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n\n**Sample augmented images (3 of each, picked at random):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/anomalygen_samples/` \u2190 3 NG + 3 paired OK files from `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/sdg/{{reconstructed_image,original_image}}/`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/mining_samples/` \u2190 first 3 images referenced in `<run>/iter1/mining_filter/mined_filtered.parquet`\n\n**RCA outputs (data files; markdown report is optional):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_gaps.parquet` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/kpi_gaps.parquet`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_threshold.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/threshold.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_weak_breakdown.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/weak_samples_breakdown.txt`\n- (Optional) `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_RCA_report.md` if the orchestrator authored one.\n\n**Routing outputs:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_routing_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/routing_results/<timestamp>/routing_summary.txt`\n\n## Pipeline Execution granularity for this eval\nWhen rendering the Pipeline Execution table in your Step 3 summary, use EXACTLY these rows (one row per logical stage \u2014 do NOT unfold internal sub-steps):\n\n1. `Baseline Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train from scratch on the base CSV.\n2. `Baseline Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare (best_val + latest), each runs `analyze_kpi.py`; the loop picks the lower FAR@100%-recall as the baseline result.\n3. `Baseline RCA` \u2014 `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` (`gap_analysis vcn_aoi`) on baseline best-checkpoint inference.\n4. `Routing` \u2014 `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` splits `kpi_gaps.parquet` into `mining_gaps.parquet` + `anomalygen_gaps.parquet`.\n5. `AnomalyGen SDG` \u2014 the entire AnomalyGen stage as ONE row (AMP via `prep_testcase.sh` + diffusion via `run_sdg.sh`, no host-side wrappers).\n6. `Data Mining` \u2014 SigLIP embed targets + source pool + `tmm nearest_neighbors` + host-side cosine\u22650.9 filter, all in ONE row.\n7. `Data Merge` \u2014 SDG row prep + base CSV + mining pool merge \u2192 `dataset/train_combined_iter1.csv` + provenance + existence/leakage validation.\n8. `Iter1 Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train on the merged CSV.\n9. `Iter1 Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare + `analyze_kpi.py` on iter1 checkpoints.\n\nTypical columns: `Stage | Duration | Key Output / Metric`. Keep it to these 9 rows.\n\n## Expected outcome\nThe entire DEFT loop runs autonomously without human intervention \u2014 the Pre-Flight Summary approval gate is auto-approved (see \"Mandatory completion\" above) and execution proceeds directly. **KPI magnitude is not graded** \u2014 the only grading criterion is end-to-end completion. The final `deft_state.json` must show top-level `status == 'complete'` and both `iterations.baseline.status == 'complete'` and `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'`; no secondary artifact audit overrides those state fields.",
      "expected_outcome": "Full DEFT loop completes end-to-end and the final `deft_state.json` is the sole canonical completion record: top-level `status` is `complete`, both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` are `complete`, and ordered state events record the required baseline/iter1 stages through `loop_stop`. Required CI artifacts are copied as requested by the prompt, but the evaluator does not reconstruct or independently re-audit the run from them. KPI magnitude is not graded because max_iterations=1 is valid stop proof. Every piece of evidence must come from THIS run: job records minted here, logs read from those records. A report assembled from an earlier run's outputs describes work this run did not do and is a FAILURE, however complete it looks."
    },
    {
      "id": "deft-aoi-stages-on-docker",
      "prompt": "## What this eval is for\n\nDEFT AOI stages used to be documented as literal `docker run` lines, which meant\nthe loop could only ever run on docker. Each stage is now emitted as a\nplatform-neutral spec-bundle by `scripts/stage_bundle.py` and launched through\n`scripts/deft_exec.py`, which renders it for the chosen platform. This eval\nproves that path works on docker \u2014 it is a PLATFORM INTEGRATION check, not a\nmodel-quality check.\n\nRead `references/stage-execution.md` first. Do not fall back to a hand-written\n`docker run` / `kubectl run` / `srun`: bypassing `deft_exec.py` is a failure even\nif the container runs, because it proves nothing about the contract.\n\n## Part 1 \u2014 every stage renders for docker (no execution)\n\nList the stage table and, for EVERY stage in it, emit a bundle and render it for\n`docker` without launching:\n\n```bash\nAOI=\"$CI_PROJECT_DIR/skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi/scripts\"\npython3 \"$AOI/stage_bundle.py\" --list\n```\n\nSupply each stage's required `--param` values as plausible absolute paths, and a\nminimal `--spec-file` for the `mode=config` stages. Validate every bundle with\n`scripts/tao_spec_bundle.py validate` and confirm each renders. Report any stage\nthat fails to render or to validate \u2014 that is the finding, not a reason to stop.\n\n## Part 2 \u2014 one stage runs live on docker\n\nTake `anomalygen.amp` (declared `gpus=0`, so no GPU is needed) and run it end to\nend through the four verbs. Override the image so this stays CI-sized:\n\n    --image docker.io/library/bash:5.2\n\n`busybox:1.36` will NOT work here for two independent reasons: the\nspec-bundle requires a fully-qualified `registry/path:tag` and rejects a\nbare name, and the stage command is `bash -lc`, which busybox does not\nprovide.\n\nHave the stage command read its input through the exported environment and write\nthrough `$TAO_RESULTS_ROOT`, e.g.:\n\n    --arg 'set -eu; : \"${{TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR:?not exported}}\"; n=$(ls \"$TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR\" | wc -l); [ \"$n\" -gt 0 ] || {{ echo \"read 0 inputs\" >&2; exit 3; }}; printf \"amp_inputs=%s\\n\" \"$n\" > \"$TAO_RESULTS_ROOT/allocation.json\"; echo tao-stage-alive'\n\nCreate the input directory with at least one file first, so a zero count means a\nreal mount failure rather than an empty fixture.\n\nThen, using `deft_exec.py` only:\n\n1. **submit** \u2014 `--submit --bundle <file> --platform docker <ctx>`; capture the job id\n2. **status** \u2014 `--await-job <id>` to a terminal state\n3. **logs** \u2014 `--logs <id> --tail 50`; confirm the `tao-stage-alive` token\n4. **cancel** \u2014 `--cancel <id>`; on an already-finished job this must exit 0 and\n   report the existing terminal state, NOT attempt an illegal transition\n\n## What to verify and report\n\nWrite `{{artifacts_dir}}/eval_report.md` covering:\n\n- the emitted bundle for the live stage (paste it)\n- the rendered launch command for docker\n- that `TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR` was exported and the stage read a NON-ZERO count \u2014\n  a zero count with a COMPLETE record is the specific failure this checks for,\n  because an absent mount does not raise: the stage reads nothing, writes empty\n  output and exits 0, and every downstream stage treats that as real\n- `allocation.json` present under the results dir with the expected count\n- the job record's full state transitions, ending COMPLETE\n- the four verb invocations and their outputs\n- the Part 1 table: every stage, rendered yes/no, validated yes/no\n\n## Docker specifics\n\n`<ctx>` is usually empty. The eval container has the host Docker socket mounted,\nso containers are siblings on the host \u2014 any path you bind must be resolvable by\nthe host daemon, so create the input and results directories under a host-visible\npath, not inside the eval container's private filesystem.\n\nConfirm the rendered command carries the flags this platform requires and that\nthe bundle does NOT: `--shm-size`, `--user`, `--group-add`, and `HOME` / `USER` /\n`LOGNAME` / cache redirects. They are emitted by the docker renderer because\ndocker needs them; a bundle carrying them would not be portable. `USER`/`LOGNAME`\nin particular are load-bearing \u2014 torch calls `getpass.getuser()` at import, and\nan arbitrary `--user` UID has no `/etc/passwd` entry.\n\n`--rm` must NOT appear: it deletes the exit code `status()` reads.",
      "expected_outcome": "The eval succeeds when the report shows every stage in the table rendered and validated for docker (Part 1), and one stage ran live through all four verbs driven ONLY by deft_exec.py (Part 2). Specific failures: (1) any hand-written `docker run` that bypasses deft_exec.py, even if the container runs \u2014 it proves nothing about the contract; (2) a COMPLETE record whose stage read ZERO inputs, which is the silent-empty-read failure this eval exists to catch; (3) a job record left non-terminal; (4) --cancel on a finished job erroring instead of reporting the existing terminal state; (5) a stage that fails to render going unreported. KPI and model quality are not graded \u2014 this is a platform-integration check. Using the SDK (any tao_sdk import or *SDK() constructor) is a failure: this bank is SDK-free. Every piece of evidence must come from THIS run: job records minted here, logs read from those records. A report assembled from an earlier run's outputs describes work this run did not do and is a FAILURE, however complete it looks."
    },
    {
      "id": "deft-aoi-stages-on-kubernetes",
      "prompt": "## What this eval is for\n\nDEFT AOI stages used to be documented as literal `docker run` lines, which meant\nthe loop could only ever run on docker. Each stage is now emitted as a\nplatform-neutral spec-bundle by `scripts/stage_bundle.py` and launched through\n`scripts/deft_exec.py`, which renders it for the chosen platform. This eval\nproves that path works on kubernetes \u2014 it is a PLATFORM INTEGRATION check, not a\nmodel-quality check.\n\nRead `references/stage-execution.md` first. Do not fall back to a hand-written\n`docker run` / `kubectl run` / `srun`: bypassing `deft_exec.py` is a failure even\nif the container runs, because it proves nothing about the contract.\n\n## Part 1 \u2014 every stage renders for kubernetes (no execution)\n\nList the stage table and, for EVERY stage in it, emit a bundle and render it for\n`kubernetes` without launching:\n\n```bash\nAOI=\"$CI_PROJECT_DIR/skills/applications/tao-run-deft-aoi/scripts\"\npython3 \"$AOI/stage_bundle.py\" --list\n```\n\nSupply each stage's required `--param` values as plausible absolute paths, and a\nminimal `--spec-file` for the `mode=config` stages. Validate every bundle with\n`scripts/tao_spec_bundle.py validate` and confirm each renders. Report any stage\nthat fails to render or to validate \u2014 that is the finding, not a reason to stop.\n\n## Part 2 \u2014 one stage runs live on kubernetes\n\nTake `anomalygen.amp` (declared `gpus=0`, so no GPU is needed) and run it end to\nend through the four verbs. Override the image so this stays CI-sized:\n\n    --image docker.io/library/bash:5.2\n\n`busybox:1.36` will NOT work here for two independent reasons: the\nspec-bundle requires a fully-qualified `registry/path:tag` and rejects a\nbare name, and the stage command is `bash -lc`, which busybox does not\nprovide.\n\nHave the stage command read its input through the exported environment and write\nthrough `$TAO_RESULTS_ROOT`, e.g.:\n\n    --arg 'set -eu; : \"${{TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR:?not exported}}\"; n=$(ls \"$TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR\" | wc -l); [ \"$n\" -gt 0 ] || {{ echo \"read 0 inputs\" >&2; exit 3; }}; printf \"amp_inputs=%s\\n\" \"$n\" > \"$TAO_RESULTS_ROOT/allocation.json\"; echo tao-stage-alive'\n\nCreate the input directory with at least one file first, so a zero count means a\nreal mount failure rather than an empty fixture.\n\nThen, using `deft_exec.py` only:\n\n1. **submit** \u2014 `--submit --bundle <file> --platform kubernetes <ctx>`; capture the job id\n2. **status** \u2014 `--await-job <id>` to a terminal state\n3. **logs** \u2014 `--logs <id> --tail 50`; confirm the `tao-stage-alive` token\n4. **cancel** \u2014 `--cancel <id>`; on an already-finished job this must exit 0 and\n   report the existing terminal state, NOT attempt an illegal transition\n\n## What to verify and report\n\nWrite `{{artifacts_dir}}/eval_report.md` covering:\n\n- the emitted bundle for the live stage (paste it)\n- the rendered launch command for kubernetes\n- that `TAO_INPUT_DATASET_DIR` was exported and the stage read a NON-ZERO count \u2014\n  a zero count with a COMPLETE record is the specific failure this checks for,\n  because an absent mount does not raise: the stage reads nothing, writes empty\n  output and exits 0, and every downstream stage treats that as real\n- `allocation.json` present under the results dir with the expected count\n- the job record's full state transitions, ending COMPLETE\n- the four verb invocations and their outputs\n- the Part 1 table: every stage, rendered yes/no, validated yes/no\n\n## Kubernetes specifics\n\nThe eval container runs as a non-root user with the host Docker socket mounted\nand host networking, which is what makes a local cluster reachable: minikube\nbinds its API server on the host and `--network host` lets `kubectl` here reach\nit. Do not switch to bridge networking. You cannot `apt-get install`; `kubectl`\nand `minikube` are single static binaries \u2014 download them to a user-writable\ndirectory on `$PATH` if absent.\n\nPass `--ctx namespace=\u2026 --ctx mount_path=\u2026 --ctx pvc_claim=\u2026`. A pod sees ONE\nbound volume, so every declared input must live under the mounted claim \u2014 a\ndeclared input outside it is a legitimate render failure and should be reported\nas such, not worked around by rewriting the stage.\n\nConfirm the generated manifest PARSES as YAML and that `TAO_INPUT_*` appear as\n`env:` entries with `TAO_RESULTS_ROOT`. Generated YAML is indentation-sensitive,\nso parse it rather than grepping. If the stage declares a `workdir`, confirm it\nbecame `workingDir` on the container.",
      "expected_outcome": "The eval succeeds when the report shows every stage in the table rendered and validated for kubernetes (Part 1), and one stage ran live through all four verbs driven ONLY by deft_exec.py (Part 2). Specific failures: (1) any hand-written `kubectl run`/`kubectl apply` that bypasses deft_exec.py, even if the container runs \u2014 it proves nothing about the contract; (2) a COMPLETE record whose stage read ZERO inputs, which is the silent-empty-read failure this eval exists to catch; (3) a job record left non-terminal; (4) --cancel on a finished job erroring instead of reporting the existing terminal state; (5) a stage that fails to render going unreported. KPI and model quality are not graded \u2014 this is a platform-integration check. Using the SDK (any tao_sdk import or *SDK() constructor) is a failure: this bank is SDK-free. Every piece of evidence must come from THIS run: job records minted here, logs read from those records. A report assembled from an earlier run's outputs describes work this run did not do and is a FAILURE, however complete it looks."
    },
    {
      "id": "deft-loop-ag-mining-kubernetes",
      "prompt": "Run the full DEFT Loop end-to-end as a smoke test on subset data with AnomalyGen + Data Mining.\n\n## Mandatory completion\nThis eval grades end-to-end completion. Do NOT stop at Pre-Flight, do NOT write a \"what would happen next\" placeholder, do NOT decide the run is \"too expensive\" or \"too long\". Do not preemptively shorten the work.\n\n**No human is in the loop.** Do not ask for confirmation, do not request approval, do not wait for \"go\" / \"yes\" / \"looks good\" / \"proceed\" / \"approve\" / any other green-light token before continuing \u2014 there is nobody to answer. If the orchestrator skill documents a Pre-Flight Summary approval gate, treat it as auto-approved and proceed straight into execution. Print the Pre-Flight summary for the log if you like, but never block on it.\n\n**Single completion criterion.** The eval is complete if and only if the final `deft_state.json` records `status == \"complete\"` and both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` as `\"complete\"`. Those state fields are the canonical completion record; keep executing until they are all complete. Until that file shows iter1 complete, you have NOT finished the work \u2014 keep executing the next stage in the orchestrator's flow. Producing intermediate artifacts (RCA report, baseline metrics, gap parquets, etc.) is necessary but NOT sufficient; an eval that stops after baseline+RCA without running Routing \u2192 AnomalyGen \u2192 Mining \u2192 Data Merge \u2192 Iter1 Training \u2192 Iter1 Inference is INCOMPLETE and will be graded as a failure regardless of how much partial work was done. Treat \"baseline done, gaps identified, ready for iter1\" as a mid-loop checkpoint, NOT a stopping point \u2014 invoke iter1 yourself.\n\n**Final-write mandate (load-bearing).** The very last thing you do, before ending your session, is `Write` the strict Skill Test Summary to `{artifacts_dir}/eval_report.md` (header + Run callout + Verdict block + Steps 1\u20135 + `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, exactly as documented in your skill-tester instructions). If that file is missing OR does not start with `## Skill Test Summary` OR does not end with `---END-SKILL-REPORT---`, the run is graded as **Error (no report)** regardless of how much pipeline work succeeded \u2014 `RCA_Report.md`, `transcript.md`, `iter1_summary.md`, and similar are NOT substitutes. Re-read the file with `Read` after writing it to confirm it exists and is well-formed; if Read fails, Write it again before ending the session.\n\n## Plugin Installation\nThis eval depends on the `tao-skills` plugin (bundled in the `tao-skills-external` repo). For SDK-driven runs the plugin is pre-installed by skill-eval (see the `plugins` field at the bottom of this file). For interactive TUI runs install it manually:\n\n```bash\nPLUGIN_ROOT=\"${{CI_PROJECT_DIR:-$HOME/tao-skills-external}}\"\nrm -rf ~/.claude/plugins/cache/tao-skill-bank/tao-skills\n```\n\n```\n/plugin marketplace add $PLUGIN_ROOT\n/plugin install tao-skills@tao-skill-bank\n/plugin marketplace update tao-skill-bank\n```\n\n## Data download (do this FIRST)\nThis runner is a non-airgap colossus host with outbound network. `$WORKSPACE_DIR` is provided by skill-eval and is bind-mounted at the SAME absolute path on host + container so nested `docker run -v $WORKSPACE_DIR/\u2026:/\u2026` resolves correctly through the host docker daemon. Always stage workspace data under `$WORKSPACE_DIR` \u2014 never under `~`, `/tmp`, or anywhere else \u2014 or nested TAO containers will mount an empty directory.\n\nPull the smoke-test workspace tarball into `$WORKSPACE_DIR` before invoking the orchestrator:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ncd \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"\ns5cmd --profile seanlin --endpoint-url https://pdx.s8k.io cp 's3://computex/deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz' .\ntar -xzf deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz -C \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\" --strip-components=1\nrm -f \"$WORKSPACE_DIR/deft_workspace_0526.tar.gz\"\n```\n\nThe tarball expands to the layout the orchestrator skill expects (validation images, base training CSV, AnomalyGen project checkpoint, backbone, HF model cache). After extraction, do not pre-stage anything else \u2014 the orchestrator drives the rest.\n\n## Skill\nUse the `tao-run-deft-aoi` skill as the orchestrator \u2014 it drives the full DEFT loop end-to-end and invokes its sub-skills by name:\n- `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` \u2014 gap analysis (root-cause) on baseline inference\n- `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` \u2014 split RCA gaps into mining + AnomalyGen subsets\n- `tao-generate-anomalies` \u2014 diffusion-based defect inpainting (uses `metropolis_sdg.paidf_anomalygen` image from versions.yaml)\n- `tao-mine-aoi-images` \u2014 SigLIP embed-then-mine over the source pool, cosine k-NN filter\n- `tao-train-visual-changenet` \u2014 baseline + iter1 training, inference, KPI sweep\n\nFollow the orchestrator's documented Pre-Flight \u2192 execute \u2192 report flow. Resolve container images via the Pre-Flight exports (`TAO_PYT_IMAGE`, `TAO_DS_IMAGE`, `AG_IMAGE`) stamped from `versions.yaml`, or package a skill-local `scripts/resolve_versions_key.py`; do not require a helper that is not installed with the skill.\n\n## Platform \u2014 Kubernetes\n\nThis is the SAME loop as `deft-loop-ag-mining`, on a different platform, from the\nSAME stage definitions. That is the property under test: if any stage needs a\nhand-written `kubectl` or `docker run` to work here, the loop is not actually\nplatform-neutral and that is the finding.\n\nBring up a GPU-capable local cluster first. The Colossus agent has GPUs\n(`nvidia-smi -L`) and the host docker daemon already has the NVIDIA runtime \u2014\nthat is how the docker evals run TAO images with `--gpus all` \u2014 but minikube does\nNOT inherit it:\n\n**Before anything else, check the tools exist.** The runner does not ship\n`kubectl`, `minikube` or `nvidia-smi`, and you cannot `apt-get install` (no\nroot). `kubectl` and `minikube` are single static binaries \u2014 download them to a\nuser-writable directory on `$PATH` (e.g. `$HOME/.local/bin`) and `chmod +x`.\n\n**Then probe the GPU runtime BEFORE starting a cluster.** `--gpus all` needs the\nNVIDIA container runtime registered with the host docker daemon; without it\nminikube half-starts and leaves `kubelet: Stopped`, `apiserver: Stopped`, which\nreads as a Kubernetes problem rather than a missing runtime hook:\n\n```bash\ncommand -v nvidia-smi >/dev/null && nvidia-smi -L\ndocker info 2>/dev/null | grep -qi nvidia && echo \"nvidia runtime: present\" \\\n  || { echo \"nvidia runtime NOT registered with docker\"; echo \"INFRA FINDING\"; exit 1; }\n```\n\nIf the runtime is absent, STOP and report it. Do not start a cluster without\n`--gpus all` and continue \u2014 a CPU-only cluster cannot run the training stages,\nand this eval grades skipping them as a failure.\n\n**Never stage artifacts from a previous run.** If this turn could not launch,\nreport that. A report assembled from an earlier run's outputs describes work\nthis run did not do, and every stage's evidence must come from job records\nminted in THIS run.\n\n```bash\nminikube start --driver docker --container-runtime docker --gpus all\nminikube addons enable nvidia-device-plugin\nkubectl get node -o jsonpath='{.items[0].status.allocatable.nvidia\\.com/gpu}{\"\\n\"}'\n```\n\nThat last number must be non-zero before any training stage. If it is 0 after the\naddon settles, install the GPU Operator instead\n(`helm install --wait gpu-operator nvidia/gpu-operator -n gpu-operator --create-namespace`)\nand report which path worked. A CPU-only cluster is an infrastructure finding to\nreport, NOT a reason to skip the training stages and declare success.\n\nThe workspace must be reachable from inside pods, and minikube's node is a\ncontainer -- it does not automatically see `$WORKSPACE_DIR`. Prove it BEFORE\nlaunching any stage, so an unreachable workspace is not discovered after a GPU\nJob has already queued:\n\n```bash\ndocker exec minikube test -d \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\" \\\n  || { echo \"minikube node cannot see $WORKSPACE_DIR\"; exit 1; }\ndocker exec minikube df -h \"$WORKSPACE_DIR\"   # room for the workspace + base checkpoints\n```\n\nIf the node cannot see it, restart minikube with a mount for that path, or fail\nthis eval as an infrastructure finding \u2014 do not proceed. Then back a PVC with\nthat host path and give every stage the same `mount_path`:\n\n```bash\nexport PLATFORM=kubernetes\nexport PLATFORM_CTX=\"--ctx namespace=deft --ctx pvc_claim=deft-workspace \\\n  --ctx mount_path=$WORKSPACE_DIR --ctx job_dir=$WORKSPACE_DIR/.k8s\"\n```\n\n`job_dir` MUST be under `mount_path`: a config-mode stage writes its spec\nthere and the pod reads it through the single bound volume, so a job_dir\noutside it is refused at render time.\n\n```bash\n```\n\nA pod sees ONE bound volume, so every declared input must live under\n`mount_path`. An input outside it is a legitimate render failure \u2014 report it\nrather than working around it by rewriting the stage.\n\nLoad the TAO images into the cluster's daemon before the first stage\n(`minikube image load`, or `eval $(minikube docker-env)` before the pull);\notherwise every Job sits in `ImagePullBackOff` while the loop waits.\n\nTear the cluster down (`minikube delete`) when finished, pass or fail.\n\n## DEFT loop parameters\n- KPI target: `FAR < 10% at Recall = 100%`\n- Max iterations: 1\n- Training epochs: 2 per iteration\n- num_SDG: 20\n- Workspace: `$WORKSPACE_DIR` (set by skill-eval; bind-mounted at the same absolute path on host + container so docker-in-docker mounts work)\n\n## Artifacts to upload (save under {artifacts_dir})\nDo NOT upload model checkpoint files. Cherry-pick these for the MR:\n\n**KPI / metrics:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_summary.md` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/iter1_summary.md`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/DEFT_Loop_Report.html` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/DEFT_Loop_Report.html`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/deft_state.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/deft_state.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model.json` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model.json`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/best_model_inference_spec.yaml` \u2190 `$WORKSPACE_DIR/results/<run>/best_model_inference_spec.yaml`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_inference_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/summary.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_threshold_metrics.csv` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/threshold_metrics.csv`\n\n**Visualizations (PNGs from `analyze_kpi.py`):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_score_distribution.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/score_distribution_with_recall_100_threshold.png`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_confusion_matrix.png` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/inference/best_val/confusion_matrix_recall_100.png`\n\n**Sample augmented images (3 of each, picked at random):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/anomalygen_samples/` \u2190 3 NG + 3 paired OK files from `<run>/iter1/anomalygen/sdg/{{reconstructed_image,original_image}}/`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/mining_samples/` \u2190 first 3 images referenced in `<run>/iter1/mining_filter/mined_filtered.parquet`\n\n**RCA outputs (data files; markdown report is optional):**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_gaps.parquet` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/kpi_gaps.parquet`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_threshold.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/threshold.txt`\n- `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_rca_weak_breakdown.txt` \u2190 `<run>/baseline/rca_results/<timestamp>/weak_samples_breakdown.txt`\n- (Optional) `{artifacts_dir}/baseline_RCA_report.md` if the orchestrator authored one.\n\n**Routing outputs:**\n- `{artifacts_dir}/iter1_routing_summary.txt` \u2190 `<run>/iter1/routing_results/<timestamp>/routing_summary.txt`\n\n## Pipeline Execution granularity for this eval\nWhen rendering the Pipeline Execution table in your Step 3 summary, use EXACTLY these rows (one row per logical stage \u2014 do NOT unfold internal sub-steps):\n\n1. `Baseline Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train from scratch on the base CSV.\n2. `Baseline Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare (best_val + latest), each runs `analyze_kpi.py`; the loop picks the lower FAR@100%-recall as the baseline result.\n3. `Baseline RCA` \u2014 `tao-analyze-gaps-visual-changenet` (`gap_analysis vcn_aoi`) on baseline best-checkpoint inference.\n4. `Routing` \u2014 `tao-route-visual-changenet-samples` splits `kpi_gaps.parquet` into `mining_gaps.parquet` + `anomalygen_gaps.parquet`.\n5. `AnomalyGen SDG` \u2014 the entire AnomalyGen stage as ONE row (AMP via `prep_testcase.sh` + diffusion via `run_sdg.sh`, no host-side wrappers).\n6. `Data Mining` \u2014 SigLIP embed targets + source pool + `tmm nearest_neighbors` + host-side cosine\u22650.9 filter, all in ONE row.\n7. `Data Merge` \u2014 SDG row prep + base CSV + mining pool merge \u2192 `dataset/train_combined_iter1.csv` + provenance + existence/leakage validation.\n8. `Iter1 Training` \u2014 2-epoch ChangeNet train on the merged CSV.\n9. `Iter1 Inference + KPI` \u2014 two-checkpoint compare + `analyze_kpi.py` on iter1 checkpoints.\n\nTypical columns: `Stage | Duration | Key Output / Metric`. Keep it to these 9 rows.\n\n## Expected outcome\nThe entire DEFT loop runs autonomously without human intervention \u2014 the Pre-Flight Summary approval gate is auto-approved (see \"Mandatory completion\" above) and execution proceeds directly. **KPI magnitude is not graded** \u2014 the only grading criterion is end-to-end completion. The final `deft_state.json` must show top-level `status == 'complete'` and both `iterations.baseline.status == 'complete'` and `iterations.iter1.status == 'complete'`; no secondary artifact audit overrides those state fields.",
      "expected_outcome": "Full DEFT loop completes end-to-end and the final `deft_state.json` is the sole canonical completion record: top-level `status` is `complete`, both `iterations.baseline.status` and `iterations.iter1.status` are `complete`, and ordered state events record the required baseline/iter1 stages through `loop_stop`. Required CI artifacts are copied as requested by the prompt, but the evaluator does not reconstruct or independently re-audit the run from them. KPI magnitude is not graded because max_iterations=1 is valid stop proof. Additionally, this run must execute on Kubernetes, judged from per-stage evidence rather than a transcript search: every stage has a job record or state event showing it was launched by scripts/deft_exec.py with --platform kubernetes. Hand-written kubectl is EXPECTED for cluster setup and diagnosis and is not a finding; substituting it for a stage launch is. Allocatable nvidia.com/gpu must be non-zero before the first training stage. DEFT_Loop_Report.html must agree with deft_state.json -- if state is incomplete, the report must not present completion or final metric claims, since a polished report over an unfinished loop is the failure mode that looks most like success. A run that silently falls back to docker, or that skips the GPU stages because the cluster had no GPU, is a FAILURE -- the point of this eval is that the same stage definitions run here. Every piece of evidence must come from THIS run: job records minted here, logs read from those records. A report assembled from an earlier run's outputs describes work this run did not do and is a FAILURE, however complete it looks."
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [
    {
      "name": "NGC_KEY",
      "description": "NGC API key with read access to every nvcr.io org this workflow pulls from: nvcr.io/nvidia/tao/* (tao-toolkit for ChangeNet train/inference, RCA `gap_analysis vcn_aoi`, and Mining `embedding image_embeddings` / `tmm nearest_neighbors`) and nvcr.io/nv-metropolis-dev/* (metropolis-sdg/paidf-anomalygen for AnomalyGen Phase 2 AMP + Phase 3 SDG diffusion). If only NGC_API_KEY is present, Pre-Flight exports NGC_KEY from it and also exports NGC_API_KEY for TAO containers. Resolve concrete image URIs from versions.yaml."
    },
    {
      "name": "HF_TOKEN",
      "description": "HuggingFace token used for one-time pulls when base checkpoints are not pre-staged. The smoke-test workspace tarball ships the cache, so HF_TOKEN is only needed if the orchestrator detects a missing model and falls back to a runtime download."
    }
  ],
  "plugins": {
    "claude": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skills@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ],
    "codex": [
      {
        "marketplace": "${CI_PROJECT_DIR}",
        "plugin": "tao-skill-bank@tao-skill-bank"
      }
    ]
  }
}
